# Wave W17-T (Route 131): moor sand — mooring-shore sand: a warm shore sand worn by the raft town\u2019s traffic, darker worn flecks standing in short horizontal runs across the tread — rope-worn, the corridor\u2019s mooring shores where a hundred rafts have tied up and pushed off (design: the corridor\u2019s mooring shores south of Tempest Tower\u2019s island). Route 131\u2019s own sand — the fleet\u2019s only rope-worn sand: split from Route 130\u2019s bright garden-flecked shallows sand by the worn runs and the missing garden light, and from Route 127\u2019s kelp-shadowed sand by warmth (worked shore vs forest shadow).
